#: ../../source/docs/common-fettec-onewire.rst:39
#: 3c432b13e378417daca70dcad33d31f5
msgid "The protocol supports up-to 24 ESCs, but ArduPilot's device driver implementation currently limits this to 12. Connect the ``TLM`` telemetry output from the ESC to the serial ``RX`` of your flight-controller. The signal-pins ``S1``, ``S2``, ``S3``, ``S4`` from the ESC are used to receive the commands from the flight-controller, so the serial ``TX`` from the flight-controller must be connected to every signal-input in parallel. On CubeOrange the GPS2 port has been successfully tested and it is recommended that you use that serial port."
msgstr ""

